  "body": "Context: https://github.com/w3c/IndexedDB/issues/87\r\n\r\nNominally, to describe the Indexed DB behavior in browsers implied by the current spec's _\"When control is returned to the event loop, the implementation must unset the active flag.\"_ ([here](https://w3c.github.io/IndexedDB/#dom-idbdatabase-transaction)) we'd need a hook akin to the \"clean-up jobs list\" hook for FileAPI.\r\n\r\nThe [event loop processing model](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop-processing-model) would grow a new step after _6. Microtasks: Perform a microtask checkpoint._, something like:\r\n\r\n> 7. Perform each of the jobs in the post-task clean-up jobs list, and then empty the list.\r\n\r\nEvent loop would then have a definition for _post-task clean-up jobs list_ similar to the [global script clean-up jobs list](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#clean-up-after-running-script) with similar requirements (\"a clean-up job cannot run scripts, and cannot be sensitive to the order in which other clean-up jobs are executed\"). \r\n\r\nIndexed DB would invoke with:\r\n\r\n> 8. Add a step to the relevant event loop's post-task clean-up jobs list to unset transaction's active flag\r\n\r\nThere may be a better approach which is web-compatible, but tossing this out for initial discussion.",
